## [Copy link to heading](https://vercel.com/blog/ai-sdk-6#tool-improvements) Tool Improvements
### [Copy link to heading](https://vercel.com/blog/ai-sdk-6#tool-execution-approval) Tool Execution Approval
Without it, you're blindly trusting the agent on every decision.

In AI SDK 6, you get human-in-the-loop control with a single `needsApproval` flag, no custom code required.

```typescript
1import { tool } from 'ai';

2import { z } from 'zod';

3export const runCommand = tool({

4  description: 'Run a shell command',

5  inputSchema: z.object({

6    command: z.string().describe('The shell command to execute'),

7  }),

8  needsApproval: true, // Require user approval

9  execute: async ({ command }) => {

10    // Your command execution logic here

11  },

12});
```

Not every tool call needs approval. You can pass a function to `needsApproval` to decide based on the input, and store user preferences to remember approved patterns for future calls.

```typescript
1import { tool } from "ai";

2import { z } from "zod";

3const runCommand = tool({

4  description: "Run a shell command",

5  inputSchema: z.object({

6    command: z.string().describe("The shell command to execute"),

7  }),

8  needsApproval: async ({ command }) => command.includes("rm -rf"),

9  execute: async ({ command }) => {

10    /* command execution logic */

11  },

12});
```

```tsx
1import { ChatAddToolApproveResponseFunction } from 'ai';

2import { runCommand } from './tools/command-tool';

3export function CommandToolView({

4  invocation,

5  addToolApprovalResponse,

6}: {

7  invocation: UIToolInvocation<typeof runCommand>;

8  addToolApprovalResponse: ChatAddToolApproveResponseFunction;

9}) {

10  if (invocation.state === 'approval-requested') {

11    return (

12      <div>

13        <p>Run command: {invocation.input.command}?</p>

14        <button

15          onClick={() =>

16            addToolApprovalResponse({

17              id: invocation.approval.id,

18              approved: true,

19            })

20          }

21        >

22          Approve

23        </button>

24        <button

25          onClick={() =>

26            addToolApprovalResponse({

27              id: invocation.approval.id,

28              approved: false,

29            })

30          }

31        >

32          Deny

33        </button>

34      </div>

35    );

36  }

37  if (invocation.state === 'output-available') {

38    return <div>Output: {invocation.output}</div>;

39  }

40  // Handle other states...

41}

42
```

# Allow conditionally skipping tool call
```typescript
1const result = await streamText({

2  model: openai('gpt-4'),

3  messages,

4  tools: {

5    // your tools

6  },

7  experimental_repairToolCall: async ({ toolCall }) => {

8    // Check your custom flag on the toolCall

9    if (toolCall.alreadyExecuted) {

10      // Skip this tool call

11      return null;

12    }

13

14    // Otherwise, proceed normally

15    return toolCall;

16  }

17});
```

